# playpick cell: mode=menus view=820x1180,touch save=carried
#
# What no session has done before: README's "Getting better at it" section
# promises two things this job has never actually tested -- the results
# screen's own kill-to-kill comparison line ("4.2s faster than your last
# kill...") and personal bests re-announcing correctly on a second kill of
# the same boss/difficulty -- because #273 means state only ever carries
# within one playbot invocation, and no prior session pulled the same boss
# twice inside one script to get two kills to compare. This does that: kill
# Bonegrinder 10-normal, retry the identical pull, kill it again, and read
# both results screens plus (if reachable from the fight screen after a
# kill) the RECORD screen's own per-boss line in the same invocation.
open #b=marrow&s=10&h=0
tap class:warrior:arms
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
play good 110
state
shot kill1
says

tap outcome:retry
waitscreen fight 15
play good 110
state
shot kill2
says

targets
key Escape
targets
shot after-escape
